1310 BM$="Driver: The Eiffel Tower? Sure thing.":GOSUB 5100:GOSUB 9530
1320 GOSUB 6100
1350 IF A1=1 THEN GOSUB 4600:GOTO 1460
1360 A1=1:BM$="The taxi took David in front of the Eiffel Tower.\During the day it just looked like a tower of iron, but it felt completely\different now thanks to all the lights.":GOSUB 5100
1370 BM$="He considered getting to the viewing platform to have a full view of Paris,\but he wasn't really in the mood for sightseeing. He just wanted to get out\of his room.":GOSUB 5100
1450 GOSUB 4500
1460 CM=3:CM$(1)=C2$:CM$(2)=C4$:CM$(3)=C6$:GOSUB 5400
1470 IF CN=1 THEN 1500:'
1480 IF CN=2 THEN 1900:'
1490 IF CN=3 THEN 2100:'
1500 '
1510 BM$="The hill of Montmartre? Sure thing.":GOSUB 5100:GOSUB 9530
1520 GOSUB 6130
1550 IF A2=1 THEN GOSUB 4600:GOTO 1660
1560  A2=1:BM$="He arrived at Montmartre.\Due to the presence of many young artists, the shops stay open until very\late in this area.":GOSUB 5100
1570 BM$="The hill of Montmartre is where Saint Denis had been executed.\David was looking forward to seeing the windmill, but unfortunately he\was unable to.":GOSUB 5100
1580 BM$="He would have wanted to visit the old-fashioned town he always saw in\pictures, but the path was full of slopes and stairs. He couldn't afford to\exert himself so much just before the concert.":GOSUB 5100
1650 GOSUB 4500
1660 CM=3:CM$(1)=C3$:CM$(2)=C8$:CM$(3)=C1$:GOSUB 5400
1670 IF CN=1 THEN 1700:'
1680 IF CN=2 THEN 2500:'
1690 IF CN=3 THEN 1300:'
1700 '
1710 BM$="Driver: The Latin Quarter? You want to see the Pantheon, right? Got it.":GOSUB 5100:GOSUB 9530
1720 GOSUB 6160
1750 IF A3=1 THEN GOSUB 4600:GOTO 1860
1760  A3=1:BM$="The taxi left David right in front of the Pantheon. The driver explained\to him how the word was Greek for `Temple of all the gods`, and that\famous historical figures were buried inside.":GOSUB 5100
1770 BM$="David did not feel like he would get any sleep that night, so he decided to\visit the best places Paris had to offer.":GOSUB 5100
1850 GOSUB 4500
1860 CM=3:CM$(1)=C4$:CM$(2)=C6$:CM$(3)=C7$:GOSUB 5400
1870 IF CN=1 THEN 1900:'
1880 IF CN=2 THEN 2100:'
