2300 '
2310 BM$="Driver: The Basilica of the Sacred Heart? Sure thing.":GOSUB 5100:GOSUB 9530
2320 GOSUB 6250
2350 IF A7=1 THEN GOSUB 4600:GOTO 2460
2360  A7=1:BM$="The taxi left David at the Basilica of the Sacred Heart. Its\Byzantine-style white domes reflected the moonlight. By all accounts it\took 40 years to complete its construction, but it was definitely worth":GOSUB 5100:BM$="the time.":GOSUB 5100
2370 BM$="Seemingly, the view of Paris from the terrace is lovely, but the Sacred\Heart was closed during the night, so he could only take a look from\outside.":GOSUB 5100
2450 GOSUB 4500
2460 CM=3:CM$(1)=C1$:CM$(2)=C4$:CM$(3)=C9$:GOSUB 5400
2470 IF CN=1 THEN 1300:'
2480 IF CN=2 THEN 1900:'
2490 IF CN=3 THEN 2700:'
2500 '
2510 BM$="Driver: The Opera House? Sure thing.":GOSUB 5100:GOSUB 9530
2520 GOSUB 6280
2550 IF A8=1 THEN GOSUB 4600:GOTO 2660
2560  A8=1:BM$="David arrived at the world-renowned Opera House of Paris. The taxi\found a new customer and left.\Though he didn't enter himself, David heard that everything inside was":GOSUB 5100:BM$="gorgeous, not just the stage, but also the lounge, the corridors, even the\ceiling.":GOSUB 5100
2570 BM$="There were many young people in front of the opera house. They didn't\seem to be guests.\David decided to leave before someone recognized him.":GOSUB 5100
2650 GOSUB 4500
2660 CM=3:CM$(1)=C3$:CM$(2)=C9$:CM$(3)=C6$:GOSUB 5400
2670 IF CN=1 THEN 1700:'
2680 IF CN=2 THEN 2700:'
2690 IF CN=3 THEN 2100:'
2700 '
2710 BM$="Driver: The Vosges square? Sure thing.":GOSUB 5100:GOSUB 9530
2720 GOSUB 6310
2730 '
2740 '
2750 IF A9=1 THEN GOSUB 4600:GOTO 2860
2760  A9=1:BM$="When David arrived at the square, he was impressed by its splendor. There\was a reason the royal family of the 16th century would spend their time\here.":GOSUB 5100:BM$="Surrounded by red-brick buildings, the square felt like the courtyard of\a royal palace.":GOSUB 5100
2770 BM$="It would seem the garden was once closed to the public, but it was\currently teeming with tourists.\That was enough to bring David back from his 16th century dream and":GOSUB 5100:BM$="back into the real world.":GOSUB 5100
2850 GOSUB 4500
2860 CM=3:CM$(1)=C5$:CM$(2)=C6$:CM$(3)=C7$:GOSUB 5400
2870 IF CN=1 THEN 2900:'
2880 IF CN=2 THEN 2100:'
2890 IF CN=3 THEN 2300:'
2900 '
2910 BM$="Driver: You want to go to Rouen? Sure thing.":GOSUB 5100:GOSUB 9530:GOSUB 6340
2920 BM$="The taxi left David in Rouen. The place was virtually empty.\Even though he was sweating, David had goosebumps. He didn't know why.\Maybe it was because of the statue of Jeanne d'Arc.":GOSUB 5100
2930 BM$="It was the place where Jeanne d'Arc, the Maiden of Miracles who fought in\the Hundred Years' War during the 15th century, had been executed.\She fought for the sake of her country following the orders of her God,":GOSUB 5100:BM$="but the Inquisition, jealous of her fame, sentenced her to death. She was\burned at the stake, and joined her God in Heaven.":GOSUB 5100
2940 GOSUB 6390
2950 BM$="As he walked around Rouen, David noticed a building with an open gate.\For whatever reason, he felt compelled to enter...and so he did.":GOSUB 5100
2960 '
